 On apply, TA prints one `[applied]` or `[failed]` line per proposal. Proposals are replayed only when a person is present: from an interactive terminal, or when you pass `--replay-actions`. A non-interactive apply (a script, CI, the session auto-apply gate, the release pipeline) applies the files, prints how many external actions were not replayed, and leaves them for you to run with `ta draft apply <id> --replay-actions`. `--no-replay-actions`, or `TA_NO_REPLAY_ACTIONS=1`, turns replay off even in a terminal. `ta draft apply <id> --chain --dry-run` previews the whole chain and changes and replays nothing. A failed proposal never blocks the others or the file changes; fix the cause and re-run `ta draft apply`. Re-applying is safe: replayed proposals are recorded in `.ta/wayfinder-task-replay.log` and skipped next time, and created tasks always carry an `external_id` (derived from the goal and proposal ids when the agent did not supply one), so a task is never created twice. A project without `[plan] backend = "wayfinder"` simply skips the proposals with a log line. The Wayfinder service account needs only `member` role for these calls.
 
+#### Proposing Wayfinder Goals and KPIs in a Draft
+
+Goals, KPI metrics, datapoints and org-level KPIs follow the same rule as tasks: an agent never writes them live. It proposes them with four MCP tools, the proposals are reviewed in the goal's draft, and they are sent to Wayfinder only when the draft is applied. The chief-of-staff chat mode has no `ta_propose_*` tools at all.
+
+| Tool | What it proposes | Applied as |
+|---|---|---|
+| `ta_propose_goal_create` | A goal (`name`, `kind` required; `description`, `parent_goal_id`, `target_date` as `YYYY-MM-DD` optional) | `POST /api/projects/<id>/goals` |
+| `ta_propose_kpi_metric_create` | A KPI metric on a goal (`goal_id`, `label`, `unit`, `target`, `cadence`, `kind`, `aggregation`; `weight` and `require_gate` optional) | `POST /api/projects/<id>/goals/<goal_id>/kpi-metrics` |
+| `ta_propose_kpi_datapoint_add` | A datapoint on a metric (`metric_id`, `value`; `source` defaults to `manual`) | `POST /api/projects/<id>/kpi-metrics/<metric_id>/datapoints` |
+| `ta_propose_kpi_create` | An org-level KPI (`label`; `description`, `weight`, `project_scoped`, `created_by`, `source_ref` optional) | `POST /api/orgs/<org_id>/kpis` |
+
+Every call needs `goal_run_id`. Numbers must be finite and between -1e12 and 1e12. `kind`, `cadence` and `aggregation` accept only the values Wayfinder knows, and names, labels and descriptions have length limits. A bad proposal is refused when the agent makes it, so the reviewer never sees it. The project always comes from `[plan.wayfinder]` in `.ta/workflow.toml`; a proposal cannot name another one. With `project_scoped: true` an org KPI is attached to that project, otherwise it is org-wide.
+
+**Building a chain with `ref:<n>`.** Each of these tools returns a `ref` such as `ref:0`, the position of that proposal in the draft. A later proposal can pass it instead of an id, for example a metric with `goal_id: "ref:0"` and a datapoint with `metric_id: "ref:1"`. A ref must point at an earlier proposal of the right kind (a goal for `goal_id` and `parent_goal_id`, a metric for `metric_id`). A datapoint aimed at a `task_count` metric is refused at proposal time, because Wayfinder computes those from tasks.
+
+**What a reviewer sees.** `ta draft view <draft-id>` lists each proposal under pending actions with its own `ref:<n>`, the readable fields (name and kind, target and cadence, value and metric, KPI label and weight), and a line stating that it is sent to Wayfinder only when the draft is approved and applied. Rejecting a goal also stops every proposal that refers to it.
+
+**What apply does.** Proposals are replayed in the order they were made. Each create carries `external_id = ta_draft:<draft_id>:<n>`, where `n` is the proposal's position in the draft, so Wayfinder can recognise a repeat. `ref:<n>` is replaced by the id Wayfinder returned for that step. If a step fails, the steps that depend on it are not sent, and the message names the step that failed. Fix the cause and run `ta draft apply <draft-id>` again: steps that already succeeded are skipped (their returned ids are kept in `.ta/wayfinder-task-replay.log`, so refs still resolve) and the rest continue.
+
+Errors say which route failed and what to do:
+
+- 403 names the missing right: `tasks:write` for goals, metrics and datapoints, `kpis:manage` for org KPIs. Grant it to the service account in Wayfinder's Settings.
+- 409 is reported as a conflict with Wayfinder's own message. For a datapoint on a `task_count` metric that message says the metric does not accept datapoints; propose a different metric kind instead.
+- 401 means the service-account token is unknown or revoked; re-issue it and store it again with `ta credential add`.
+
